        <div id="regions" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">
            3. Regional Sealing Windows
          </h2>

          <p>
            The northern tier, including the upper Midwest, the Great Lakes, New England, and mountain areas, has the shortest season. In much of that region, reliable conditions run from roughly late May into mid-September. Late August and early September are often the sweet spot: warm days, cooler but still adequate nights, and less rain than late spring. After mid-September the margin shrinks quickly as nights get colder.
          </p>

          <p>
            The mid-Atlantic, central states, and the lower Midwest have a longer window, typically from about May into early October. Summer humidity can slow drying, so drier spells in late spring and early fall tend to give the best results. Watch for pop-up summer thunderstorms and plan around them.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Southeast and Gulf Coast can seal for much of the year, but summer brings high humidity and almost daily afternoon storms. Spring and fall are usually better, with lower humidity and more stable weather. The desert Southwest has the opposite problem: very hot summer pavement. Spring and fall are generally the better seasons there, and in summer an early-morning start is close to mandatory.
          </p>

          <p>
            The Pacific Northwest and coastal Northern California have a short, dependable window: dry summers, wet the rest of the year. July through early September is typically the best time, before fall rains begin. Coastal fog and marine humidity can slow drying even in summer, so pick days with sun and a dry forecast for the following day as well.
          </p>

          <div class="overflow-hidden border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl my-8">
            <div class="overflow-x-auto">
              <table class="w-full text-left">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50 border-b border-gray-200">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Region</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Typical Best Window</th>
                    <th class="px-4 py-4 font-bold text-gray-600 text-sm">Watch For</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                  <tr class="bg-white border-b border-gray-100">
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 font-black text-gray-900">Upper Midwest, Northeast, mountains</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Roughly late May to mid-September</td>
                    <td class="px-4 py-4 text-gray-700">Cold nights at both ends of the season</td>
